{"cmd":"meta","title":"Project Structure Map"}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_program_goals","type":"group","data":{"label":"Program Targets & KPIs (Early Builders / Developer Network)","icon":"fa-solid fa-bullseye","color":"#FDEDF5","borderColor":"#E5007D","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_program_overview","type":"card","group":"group_program_goals","data":{"title":"Early Builders / Developer Network Program","description":"Think4Ever runs a developer outreach program in Colombia called Early Builders / Developer Network. Developers and IT leads are invited, sign up through a HubSpot form, receive platform credits, and are expected to build a real project and publish content about it. This dashboard is the Research team's read-only prototype for tracking the program. It covers invitations, sign-ups, credit grants, activity, and builder deliverables. The program configuration lives in dashboard.json.program: name, signupTarget=200, accountCapacity=300, ceoTarget=null and country=Colombia.","tags":["domain:program-management","role:research","role:program-manager","entity:program","tech:prototype"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/index.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_target_cards","type":"card","group":"group_program_goals","data":{"title":"Target Indicators (Close Target, Capacity, CEO Target)","description":"The overview shows three separate goal cards so that stakeholders do not mix up different targets. (1) Developer Network close target: the signedUp funnel value compared with signupTarget (200). It shows a progress bar and a percentage capped at 100%. (2) Early Builders approved capacity: 300 accounts, shown as a separate indicator that is explicitly not the close target. (3) CEO target: always shown as 'Pending / Not confirmed yet' because ceoTarget is null. Business rule: the sign-up total comes from the funnel signedUp stage, not from counting builder rows. In the demo data this is 6 of 200, or 3%.","tags":["domain:kpi","entity:program","flow:goal-tracking","role:executive","role:research"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/index.html","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_active_definition","type":"card","group":"group_program_goals","data":{"title":"Builder Activation Business Rules","description":"This card captures the core business definitions used to judge builder success. A builder is Active only when they have a real project (projects > 0) AND published content (both contentUrl and contentAt are set). Day 0 is the credit grant date (creditsGrantedAt). Builders without a grant date are excluded from the progress metrics and show 'No date'. The day count is floor((snapshotAt - grantDate at noon Bogotá time) / 1 day), with a minimum of 0. Day-14 progress is day/14, capped at 100%. The summary cards show four metrics: Active; Within 14 days (granted builders with day < 14); Content missing (has a project, no content); and Project missing (projects = 0). The follow-up list shows up to 5 granted builders who are not yet active.","tags":["domain:builder-engagement","entity:builder","flow:day14-activation","role:program-manager"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_activation","type":"note","group":"group_program_goals","data":{"text":"**Flow: Builder Day-14 Activation**\n1. Builder signs up (signedUpAt set; stage = Inscrito).\n2. The development/credits team grants 2000 credits (creditsGrantedAt = Day 0).\n3. Builder signs in and consumes credits (signIns, lastSignIn, creditsUsed). Stage moves to En progreso.\n4. Builder creates a project (projects ≥ 1).\n5. Builder publishes a post or video (contentUrl + contentAt). Stage becomes Activo.\n6. The dashboard tracks day N/14 from the grant date. Granted builders who are not active appear in 'Needs follow-up'.\n\n**Stages:** Invitado → Inscrito → En progreso → Activo\n**Roles:** Builder (external), Program manager/Research (observer)\n**Edge cases:** no grant date → excluded from Day-14 metrics; day is clamped at ≥0; progress is capped at 100%","color":"#E7F6F0","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_invitations","type":"group","data":{"label":"Invitation & Enrollment Funnel","icon":"fa-solid fa-envelope-open-text","color":"#EEF3FF","borderColor":"#5476BB","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_funnel","type":"card","group":"group_invitations","data":{"title":"Invitation Funnel Visualization","description":"Shows the six-stage outreach funnel. In the demo data the stages are: invited/Contactados 160 → sent 120 → delivered 112 → responded 34 → accepted 18 → signedUp 6. Each step shows its absolute count and its step conversion (value / previous stage). The first step is labeled '100% of start', and the bar width is the share of the first stage. A Math.max(1, …) guard prevents division by zero. The funnel appears both on the overview and as cards in the Invitations view. The view notes that the unified prospect list comes before the HubSpot form. Source rule: email states may only be marked automatic after the connection is validated, and the prototype never simulates sends or replies.","tags":["domain:outreach","entity:funnel-stage","flow:invitation","integration:hubspot","role:marketing"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/index.html","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_funnel","type":"table","group":"group_invitations","data":{"name":"funnel (dashboard.json)","columns":[{"name":"key","type":"STRING","pk":true},{"name":"label","type":"STRING"},{"name":"value","type":"INT"}],"description":"Ordered array of aggregate counts for invitation stages: invited, sent, delivered, responded, accepted, signedUp. Order matters because conversion is computed against the previous element. The signedUp value drives the close-target KPI. In production the invited, sent, delivered, responded and accepted stages would come from the invitation list and HubSpot email state, and signedUp from HubSpot forms or PostHog.","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_invitation","type":"note","group":"group_invitations","data":{"text":"**Flow: Invitation → Enrollment**\n1. A prospect is added to the unified invitation list (email, date, channel, status). Channels: LinkedIn, GitHub, Referido, Instagram, X.\n2. The invitation email is sent and its delivery is tracked.\n3. The prospect replies and accepts.\n4. The prospect submits the HubSpot enrollment form, carrying t4e_program and t4e_ref_key.\n5. The PostHog sign-up event confirms the account (signedUp).\n\n**Data:** funnel counts; builder.refKey, channel, invitedAt, signedUpAt\n**Rules:** each stage keeps its own source and denominator; there is no simulated email state","color":"#DDF4FF","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/index.html","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_builders","type":"group","data":{"label":"Builder Tracking","icon":"fa-solid fa-users","color":"#E7F6F0","borderColor":"#178B67","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_builders","type":"table","group":"group_builders","data":{"name":"builders (dashboard.json)","columns":[{"name":"id","type":"STRING (EB-xxx)","pk":true},{"name":"email","type":"STRING (masked)"},{"name":"profile","type":"STRING (Developer|IT Lead)"},{"name":"city","type":"STRING"},{"name":"refKey","type":"STRING (t4e_ref_key)"},{"name":"channel","type":"STRING"},{"name":"stage","type":"ENUM Invitado|Inscrito|En progreso|Activo"},{"name":"invitedAt","type":"DATE"},{"name":"signedUpAt","type":"DATE|''"},{"name":"creditsGrantedAt","type":"DATE|'' (Day 0)"},{"name":"credits","type":"INT"},{"name":"creditsUsed","type":"INT"},{"name":"lastSignIn","type":"DATE|''"},{"name":"signIns","type":"INT"},{"name":"projects","type":"INT"},{"name":"contentUrl","type":"URL|''"},{"name":"contentAt","type":"DATE|''"}],"description":"Per-builder record that combines several future sources into one row: HubSpot (email, refKey, signup), PostHog (sign-ins, projects), the credits feed (grant date, credits used), and the content registry (URL, date). Emails are masked (b***01@example.test) to avoid exposing PII. refKey can be shared by several builders (for example DEMO-REF-01), which shows referral attribution. The demo contains 8 synthetic Colombian builders. Empty strings mean the milestone has not been reached.","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_builders_view","type":"card","group":"group_builders","data":{"title":"Builders List View (Search & Stage Filter)","description":"The detailed table that program managers use to follow each builder's enrollment, activity, credits and deliverables. Columns: ID with masked email, profile, stage pill, sign-up date, credits with credits used, projects with sign-in count and last sign-in, and refKey with channel. Free-text search is case-insensitive and matches id, refKey and email. The stage dropdown is filled dynamically from the distinct stages in the data. An empty result shows 'No builders match those filters'. The nav badge shows the total builder count.","tags":["domain:builder-engagement","entity:builder","role:program-manager","flow:builder-monitoring"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/index.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_followup","type":"card","group":"group_builders","data":{"title":"Needs Follow-up Table","description":"Overview table listing up to 5 builders who have received credits but are not yet active (missing a project or published content). Each row shows the stage, Day 0 grant date with days elapsed, project status (Created/Pending), content status (Published/Pending), and a mini progress track of day/14. The goal is to help the program team nudge builders before the 14-day window closes.","tags":["domain:builder-engagement","entity:builder","flow:day14-activation","role:program-manager"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/index.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_sources","type":"group","data":{"label":"Data Sources & Integrations (Planned)","icon":"fa-solid fa-database","color":"#FFF5DF","borderColor":"#A76C11","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"tbl_sources","type":"table","group":"group_sources","data":{"name":"sources (dashboard.json)","columns":[{"name":"name","type":"STRING","pk":true},{"name":"purpose","type":"STRING"},{"name":"state","type":"ENUM Pendiente|Manual|Conectado"},{"name":"method","type":"STRING"},{"name":"lastSync","type":"STRING"},{"name":"needs","type":"STRING"}],"description":"Catalog of the data connections the dashboard needs. The Sources view renders it as status cards, with the state translated to Pending, Manual or Connected. Every connection in the demo is unconnected. The catalog documents what each integration requires before real data can flow.","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_src_hubspot","type":"card","group":"group_sources","data":{"title":"HubSpot (Pending)","description":"Planned read-API source for the enrollment form, contacts and invitation or email status. It needs a private app token with contacts, forms and email scopes. It would feed the funnel sent, delivered, responded, accepted and signedUp stages, as well as builder email and refKey (t4e_program, t4e_ref_key).","tags":["integration:hubspot","domain:outreach","entity:contact","tech:rest-api"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_src_posthog","type":"card","group":"group_sources","data":{"title":"PostHog (Pending)","description":"Planned query-API source for sign-up, sign-in, project creation and first-touch UTMs. It needs a read API key, host and project ID. It would feed signIns, lastSignIn, projects and channel attribution. PostHog account IDs must be reconciled with HubSpot identities.","tags":["integration:posthog","domain:product-analytics","entity:builder","tech:rest-api"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_src_manual","type":"card","group":"group_sources","data":{"title":"Manual Feeds: Credits, Invitation List, Published Content","description":"Three sources are planned as controlled manual imports. (1) Development/credits: a daily export of grant date, activity and consumption per account. It needs a defined schema and a per-account feed, and it sets Day 0. (2) Invitation list: a controlled CSV/XLSX unified list with email, date, channel and status, covering contacts made before the form. (3) Published content: a registry of public URL, platform and date that validates the builder deliverable and therefore the Active status.","tags":["integration:file-import","entity:credit-grant","entity:invitation","entity:content","flow:data-ingestion"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_src_ga4","type":"card","group":"group_sources","data":{"title":"GA4 (Pending)","description":"Planned source for landing-page sessions and UTMs. It would use an existing connector if one is available, and needs a property ID and a service account. It supports marketing attribution for invitation channels.","tags":["integration:ga4","domain:marketing-analytics"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/data/dashboard.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_go_live","type":"note","group":"group_sources","data":{"text":"**Flow: Moving from Demo to Real Data (from README)**\n1. Implement server-side, read-only connectors inside server.js, following the data-connections plan (2026-11-05).\n2. Keep credentials in the service only, never in public/, data/ or the repository.\n3. Reconcile source identities across HubSpot, PostHog and the credits feed.\n4. Validate t4e_program, t4e_ref_key, PostHog account IDs, credit grant dates, invitation statuses and publication URLs.\n5. Only then use the metrics operationally.\n\n**Not yet implemented:** authentication, durable storage, scheduled imports, live connectors. Not connected: Outlook or the Think4Ever portal.","color":"#FFF5DF","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"group_platform","type":"group","data":{"label":"Dashboard Platform (Server & UI Shell)","icon":"fa-solid fa-server","color":"#F2F3F5","borderColor":"#30213F","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/server.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/index.html"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_server","type":"card","group":"group_platform","data":{"title":"Local Node HTTP Server","description":"A dependency-free Node 18+ server (node:http) bound to 127.0.0.1 on PORT, default 3016, so it is reachable only from the local machine. It serves the demo fixture API, a health check and static UI files from public/. Every response is sent with these security headers: X-Content-Type-Options nosniff, Referrer-Policy no-referrer and Cache-Control no-store. Only GET is accepted; any other method returns 405. Static serving decodes and normalizes the path, strips leading slashes and '..' segments, and rejects anything outside public/ with 403 to prevent path traversal. A missing file returns 404. The server shuts down gracefully on SIGINT and SIGTERM. This is the planned home for future credentialed connectors.","tags":["tech:nodejs","tech:http","domain:platform","integration:filesystem"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/server.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/package.json"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_dashboard","type":"api","group":"group_platform","data":{"method":"GET","path":"/api/dashboard","description":"Returns the full dashboard snapshot that drives every view. The file data/dashboard.json is read synchronously on each request, so edits to the fixture show up on reload. The response contains mode, snapshotAt (cutoff timestamp), program, funnel, builders and sources. If the fixture cannot be read, the endpoint returns a 500 error. The frontend replaces the content area with an error banner on failure.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ mode:'demo', snapshotAt, program{name,signupTarget,accountCapacity,ceoTarget,country}, funnel[], builders[], sources[] } | 500 { error:'Demo data unavailable' }"},"auth":"none (localhost-only binding; auth not implemented)","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/server.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_health","type":"api","group":"group_platform","data":{"method":"GET","path":"/health","description":"Liveness probe that confirms the prototype server is running and reports that it is in demo mode. This endpoint does not touch the data file.","params":[],"response":{"status":200,"body":"{ status:'ok', mode:'demo' }"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/server.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"api_static","type":"api","group":"group_platform","data":{"method":"GET","path":"/* (static)","description":"Serves index.html, app.js and styles.css from public/. The path / maps to index.html. The content type is chosen from the file extension; unknown extensions are sent as application/octet-stream. Any method other than GET returns 405.","params":[{"name":"path","type":"string","required":true}],"response":{"status":200,"body":"file contents | 403 Forbidden (traversal) | 404 Not found | 405 Method not allowed"},"auth":"none","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/server.js"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_spa","type":"card","group":"group_platform","data":{"title":"Dashboard SPA (Navigation, i18n, Rendering)","description":"A vanilla-JS single-page app with Think4Ever branding. It shows a read-only 'Research' user profile and four views: Overview, Builders, Invitations and Data sources. Navigation uses data-view and data-go attributes to toggle panels. Spanish is the default and English can be selected through a language picker. The i18n dictionary covers all labels, the stage names (Activo→Active and so on) and dates formatted for the es-CO or en-US locale in the America/Bogota timezone. Every interpolated value passes through esc() to prevent XSS. The Refresh button and the period filter (all, 30 or 14 days) only show a toast explaining that the demo cannot sync and that counts are fixed. A dismissible demo banner states that HubSpot, PostHog and the portal are not connected. The layout is responsive: the sidebar collapses at 1050px and below 760px a mobile layout hides it.","tags":["tech:vanilla-js","tech:i18n","domain:ui","role:research","security:xss-escaping"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/index.html","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/styles.css"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"node_security","type":"card","group":"group_platform","data":{"title":"Security & Privacy Posture","description":"Summary of the prototype's current security measures. Only synthetic data with masked emails is used. The server binds to localhost only. HTML output is escaped, path traversal is guarded, the server sends nosniff and no-referrer headers, and responses are not cached. The policy shown in the UI and the README is that credentials must live in the server-side service, never in the frontend, the repository or the data files. Gaps remain: there is no authentication or role enforcement (the 'read only' label is cosmetic), and styles.css loads Google Fonts from an external host.","tags":["domain:security","role:research","tech:http-headers"],"sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/server.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/styles.css"]}}
{"cmd":"add","id":"flow_dashboard_load","type":"note","group":"group_platform","data":{"text":"**Flow: Dashboard Load & Interaction**\n1. User runs `node server.js` (npm start) and opens http://127.0.0.1:3016.\n2. The server serves index.html, app.js and styles.css.\n3. app.js fetches GET /api/dashboard, and the server reads the dashboard.json fixture.\n4. render() runs translatePage, then renderSummary (targets, funnel, activation cards, follow-ups), then renderBuilders, renderInvitations and renderSources.\n5. Navigation, language toggle, search and filter all re-render on the client.\n6. Refresh and the period filter show a toast only, because no sync happens.\n\n**Errors:** fetch failure → error banner asking the user to start the server from the prototype folder","color":"#F2F3F5","sourceFiles":["early-builders-dashboard-prototype/public/app.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/server.js","early-builders-dashboard-prototype/README.md"]}}
